<title>UK: EdF ups five-year Eurobond to $600 million.</title>
<headline>EdF ups five-year Eurobond to $600 million.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been increased to $600 million from $500 million, joint lead managers J.P. Morgan Securities and SBC Warburg said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The deal was launched on Tuesday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   ELECTRICITE DE FRANCE</p>
<p> AMT	  $600 MLN  COUPON     6.625     MATURITY    24.JUN.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.24    PAY DATE    24.JUN.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    99.615    SPREAD	+12 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS US/GB/FR</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  YES	 FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  FRANCE    TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.50 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 31.MAY.02</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658  </p>
<p> NOTES	NEW PAPER HAS 101.312 ISSUE PRICE AND 99.687 REOFFER</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
